# Keeps the build context small, and keeps secrets out of it.
#
# Both Dockerfiles copy explicit paths (backend/app, index.js) rather than
# `COPY . .`, so nothing below is in an image today. This file is the second
# line of defence: the day somebody adds a `COPY . .`, a real WhatsApp session
# and a .env full of credentials would otherwise walk straight into a layer.
#
# It is also a large speed win. Without it the context is ~1.1GB - two
# virtualenvs, two node_modules trees and the git history - all of it sent to
# the Docker daemon on every single build.

# --- secrets. never in an image, never in a layer cache ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# A real WhatsApp login. Anyone holding this folder can read the account's
# messages. It belongs in a mounted volume, never in an image.
whatsapp-bridge/auth_info/

# --- dependencies, rebuilt inside the image ---
backend/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# --- build output and caches ---
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.voice-cache/
.cache/
**/.DS_Store

# --- not needed at runtime ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
*.md
!README.md
*.pdf
scripts/verify/
backend/tests/
.claude/
*.log

# --- the dashboard is not in either image; it deploys to Vercel ---
frontend/
